      While homeowners often use "shiplap" as a catch-all term for horizontal wall boards, true historic shiplap, modern nickel-gap boards, and tongue-and-groove (T&amp;G) millwork feature distinct interlocking profiles, fastening requirements, and seasonal expansion tolerances.
    </p>

